recipe plugin for DokuWiki

Wrap a standard DokuWiki list of ingredients in a <recipe> tag. The plugin
turns it into an interactive card that:

  * auto-detects common cooking units (cups, oz, lb, tsp, tbsp, pint, …)
  * converts them to metric (g / kg and ml / l)
  * lets the reader change the number of servings and rescales every amount

Syntax
------

  <recipe 4>
    * 2 cups flour
    * 3 oz butter
    * 1 1/2 tsp salt
    * 200 g sugar
    * 3 eggs
  </recipe>

The number after "recipe" is how many servings the listed amounts produce.
An optional title can be given as well:

  <recipe 12 title="Grandma's Cookies">
    * ...
  </recipe>

Amounts may be written as integers, decimals (2.5 or 2,5), fractions (1/2),
mixed numbers (1 1/2), unicode fractions (1½) or ranges (2-3 cups). Lines
without a recognisable amount (e.g. "salt to taste") are left untouched.

Without JavaScript the reader still sees the plain, server-rendered list.

All conversion and rescaling happens client-side in a modern Web Component,
so pages stay cacheable and the wiki server does no per-request maths.

Configuration
-------------

  defaultservings  servings assumed when the tag omits a number (default 1)
  showoriginal     show the original amount as a hover tooltip (default on)

----
Installed as a DokuWiki plugin. See https://www.dokuwiki.org/plugins for
details on installing plugins.

